**Q1: 178, 200, 146, 174, 124, 166, 132, 134, 140, 182**

These are all **even numbers**. If you divide each by 2, you get:
89, 100, 73, 87, 62, 83, 66, 67, 70, 91

The original numbers range from **124 to 200**, with a mean of approximately **157.6**.

---

**Q2: 103, 101, 197, 151, 127, 137, 179, 199, 191, 109**

These are all **prime numbers**. They are all primes between 100 and 200. Specifically, they are 10 of the 21 primes in that range (the missing primes in that interval are 107, 113, 163, 167, and 173).

The numbers range from **101 to 199**, with a mean of approximately **144.5**. [end of text]


